+# Arena damage transition research AIR
+
+`arena_damage_air.rs` compiles actual native integer AIR equations for one ordered damage application in the current `arena-core` reference kernel. It remains research-only. By itself it adds no execution adapter, profile ID, wire message, verifier dispatch or custody authority. The separate unregistered native-STARK source harness linked below uses these equations; qualification remains false.
+
+All 17 inputs have emitted integer interval or Boolean equations: current health/stamina; candidate damage; guarding and guard age; attacker/victim slots; two direction components; each participant's horizontal position; and claimed next health/stamina, dealt damage and lethal flag. The compiler derives the facing dot product and strict positive test from bounded direction and position inputs. It constrains guard/parry bypass for self-damage (self-damage still applies), the inclusive eight-tick parry window, twenty-stamina parry, ten-stamina half damage rounded upward, overkill cap, no damage processing for already-zero health, and a lethal flag only on a positive-to-zero health transition. Every conditional selection uses an explicitly Boolean-constrained selector. Claimed outputs are equated to the computations.
+
+The tests cover threshold/rounding boundaries, zero damage, overkill, already-dead health, self damage, back/parallel facing, two-axis facing cancellation, forged lethal/health/stamina/damage outputs, modified intermediate facing and branch witness columns, non-Boolean conditions, and out-of-range assignments. Native core compilation/testing is required before treating these as verified results; merely constructing an honest witness is insufficient.
+
+Composition remains mandatory. The integrated FPS relation must prove canonical control bytes and original roster identity; direction from yaw/pitch; movement/collision-derived positions; valid selected weapon and immutable damage; attack eligibility, charge/cooldown/stamina; trace-complete ordered nearest visible victim or projectile/explosion generation; initial-state and next-row linkage; health/alive/respawn consistency; teams, attribution and assist history; objective/terminal rules; exact NFT/bond admission; and every death allocation. A prover may freely vary this isolated slice's inputs unless the parent relation binds them. In particular, this slice does not prove that an attack occurred, cannot authenticate a caller-provided direction, and cannot authorize XOR slashing.
+
+The eventual profile must bind this source and the checked/compiler source, frozen reference rules and catalog, exact protocol domain, source hashes, field/range schedule and complete public inputs before any registration/qualification. No host-side reported-kill list substitutes for these obligations.
+
+`arena_aim_air.rs` additionally constrains the reference kernel's complete Q15 yaw/pitch direction formula, including unsigned-turn wrapping, the Bhaskara sine ratio, signed truncation, pitch projection and exact three-component output. Its controls remain unauthenticated until bound into the parent execution relation. It is test-only and adds no verifier registration.
+
+The checked variable-divisor helper emits explicit operand, quotient and remainder interval equations, excludes a zero divisor, enforces `n=q*d+r` and `0 <= r < d`, and rejects unsafe construction bounds before mutating the graph. Reconstructed values are bounded below 2^49 to exclude Goldilocks modular aliases. Adversarial tests include internally recomputed witnesses that satisfy the reconstruction equation with a false quotient, negative/out-of-range remainder or fractional field quotient; these are rejected by the interval/integrality constraints.
+
+Run `python3 scripts/check_arena_damage_air.py` for the isolated source harness after building workspace dependencies. It includes the actual integer compiler, checked helper and relation files and extracts the exact native base-field implementation, recording source hashes under `target/arena-air-research/results.log`. The current run passes 25 tests, including damage, aiming, bounded geometry, nearest eligible hit selection and variable-division cases. This is not the full core test suite or a STARK proof.
+
+The shared test-only aim and geometry appenders now compose in [`arena_hit_air.rs`](arena_hit_air.rs). See [nearest eligible hit arithmetic](ARENA_HIT_AIR.md) for exact wall/player tie rules, input order and per-attacker snapshot obligations, and [bounded geometry](ARENA_GEOMETRY_AIR.md) for the millimetre coordinate domain and clipping proof. These components remain unqualified.
+
+A separate [native STARK research experiment](ARENA_DAMAGE_STARK_RESEARCH.md)
+uses this exact damage AIR with the actual execution backend. It covers one fixed
+public damage/parry transition only; it does not compose hit selection or qualify
+a game proof. Its proof measurements are distinct from these equation tests.
