+# Arena nearest eligible hit research AIR
+
+`arena_hit_air.rs` composes the existing aiming and bounded segment/AABB
+equations in one native arithmetic graph. It follows the `Melee | Hitscan`
+branch of the current Arena reference `simulation.rs`, after an attack has been
+initiated. It is test-only and adds no profile, verifier registration, chain
+authority, or cryptographic qualification.
+
+## Exact relation and input order
+
+The roster size (1–12), wall count (0–32), and original attacker slot are fixed
+when the graph is compiled. They are not witness-selected padding or subsets.
+The parent must bind them to the complete original roster and map.
+
+| Order | Input | Emitted constraint |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 1 | Whether this is a team mode | Boolean |
+| 2 | Whether this is a melee attack | Boolean |
+| 3 | Selected weapon range | Integer, 1–70,000 mm |
+| 4–5 | Attacker yaw and pitch | Integers, 0–65,535 and −16,384–16,384 |
+| Next, for every original roster slot | Position x/y/z, team, alive, spawn-protection ticks | Position integers within ±2^20 mm; team 0/1; Boolean alive; protection integer 0–65,535 |
+| Last, for every wall | Minimum x/y/z, maximum x/y/z | Integers within ±2^20 mm and ordered bounds |
+
+All positions, wall boxes, derived ray endpoints, and derived body boxes must fit
+the geometry domain ±2^20 **millimetres**, about ±1.05 km. Positions near that
+boundary can fail because an eye/ray/body extension would leave it. Current
+reference map bounds and weapon ranges fit comfortably within the domain.
+
+The attacker must be alive. Its ray starts at position plus `(0,0,1400)` mm and
+ends after exact Q15 yaw/pitch direction multiplied by the selected range and
+divided by 32767 with truncation toward zero. Direction is derived by the shared
+`arena_aim_air::direction_v1`; neither a caller-provided direction nor reported
+intersection can replace those equations. Every wall/body intersection uses the
+shared `arena_geometry_air::intersect_v1` in the same graph and from/to columns.
+
+Walls are considered first. The initial nearest value is `Q20+1`; every
+intersected wall can lower it. A player is eligible only when its original slot
+differs from the attacker, it is alive, its protection counter is zero, and its
+team differs in team modes. In non-team modes equal team tags do not matter.
+Ineligible player bodies do not block the ray. The reference checks `alive`,
+not a separately supplied health predicate, at this stage.
+
+Player boxes are derived from position with ±350 mm in x/y and height 1700 mm.
+Melee adds exactly 180 mm to x/y radii; it expands neither wall boxes nor z.
+Eligible players are processed in ascending original roster order and replace
+the current target only when their intersection fraction is **strictly less**
+than the nearest value. Thus walls win wall/player ties, lower roster slots win
+player/player ties, and a closer later slot replaces a farther earlier one.
+The segment endpoint at exactly `Q20` is hittable when no wall ties or precedes it.
+
+Outputs are a Boolean hit, target slot encoded as `slot+1` (zero for no target),
+and nearest target fraction (canonical zero for no target). Every range,
+eligibility predicate, selector, intersection, and derived output is constrained
+by equations. There is no free reported hit bit or target fraction.
+
+## Parent binding obligations
+
+This slice does not prove that firing was legal. The parent must bind team mode,
+attack kind and range to the admitted mode and immutable weapon catalog; bind the
+attacker slot, yaw/pitch, all positions/alive/protection/team fields and complete
+wall list to their original authenticated sources; and prove input bytes,
+movement/collision, ability effects, ownership/class restrictions, cooldown,
+guarding, stamina, charging and the chosen FIRE/MELEE action.
+
+The supplied state must be the exact **per-attacker selection snapshot**:
+movement has occurred, earlier slots' abilities/attack mutations have occurred,
+and the current attacker has initiated its shot. In particular, firing removes
+its spawn protection, while later slots may still be protected. Damage is
+gathered before being applied, preserving mutual kills. Treating every attack as
+reading an arbitrary common pre-tick snapshot would not match the kernel.
+
+The parent must then join this target to immutable weapon damage, ordered damage
+application, parry/health/alive/death transitions, attribution, resources and
+terminal allocation. Projectile/explosion selection has different rules and is
+not represented here. A malicious prover can vary any unbound legal-range input
+in this isolated relation; local equations do not authenticate custody or
+authorize an XOR slash.
+
+## Focused evidence
+
+`python3 scripts/check_arena_damage_air.py` includes the actual shared helper,
+aim, geometry, damage and hit sources plus the exact native Goldilocks field.
+The aggregate source harness passes **25 tests**, including all prior aiming and
+geometry adversarial tests. Hit tests cover wall/player and player/player ties,
+unordered multiple occluders, exact range endpoints, no target, self exclusion,
+dead/protected/allied bodies that do not occlude, FFA team-tag behavior, melee XY
+expansion without wall/z expansion, 105 yaw/pitch/attacker combinations against an
+independent direct integer reference, closest-later-slot selection, and the final
+slot of a full 12-player roster.
+
+Adversarial native field assignments recompute downstream auxiliaries after
+forging target/hit/fraction/nearest, direction/endpoints, eligibility, wall/body
+intersection results, or fractional selectors. Invalid input domains, reversed
+wall bounds and a dead attacker also reject. Source hashes are recorded in
+`target/arena-air-research/results.log`. These source-level equation tests are not
+the complete Core test suite, an end-to-end game STARK, or release qualification.
+
+## Compiled native proof-layout feasibility gate
+
+`python3 scripts/check_arena_hit_stark_feasibility.py --dependency-manifest
+target/arena-damage-stark-research/build-only-pins.json` compiles this exact AIR
+and the native aggregate STARK layout/codec with pinned workspace rlibs. It does
+not call a prover, register a profile, or create a valid hit or kill proof. It
+source-seals the complete checkout, dependencies and compiler before and after
+the run and places artifacts in an exclusive ignored target directory. The
+successful 2026-09-23 run is
+`target/arena-hit-stark-feasibility/runs/layout-fmdzahmd/`; its
+`run-status.json` says `compiled_layout` and `proof_verified:false`.
+
+With the retained 8,192-row, 136-query, eightfold-LDE native geometry and the
+current 4 MiB execution-proof envelope, the **mandatory current/next trace
+openings alone** exceed the cap. Each query encodes two full-width base rows and
+two full-width auxiliary rows as canonical eight-byte Goldilocks fields. Thus
+`136 × 2 × (base width + auxiliary width) × 8` is a lower bound even before
+Merkle paths, FRI, DEEP, transcript data, or an envelope. The native
+`maximum_encoded_proof_with_deep_bytes_v1` supplies a separate conservative
+upper bound; it is not a measured proof size.
+
+| Shape | Hit AIR columns / constraints | Mandatory trace openings | Native maximum encoded wire | Dense base LDE matrix |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| One player, no walls (cannot hit another player) | 5,669 / 6,264 | 12,609,920 B | 13,832,192 B | 2,976,382,976 B |
+| Two players, no walls | 9,143 / 10,109 | 20,169,344 B | 21,613,952 B | 4,797,759,488 B |
+| Two players, three walls | 19,613 / 21,686 | 42,952,064 B | 45,066,752 B | 10,287,054,848 B |
+| Twelve players, four walls | 57,836 / 63,988 | 126,125,312 B | 130,686,272 B | 30,326,915,072 B |
+
+The matrix figures are exact arithmetic lower bounds for one dense base field
+evaluation matrix at 65,536 LDE rows, not observed process peaks. Auxiliary
+columns, fixed columns, masks, commitments, FRI and scratch require more memory.
+The three-wall case matches the current Nyaagyu Estate geometry; the four-wall
+case matches each other current Arena map. Source-level `public_inputs` counts
+are 5 + 6 per player + 6 per wall, but this shape probe does **not** add public
+binding constraints. In a real profile, authenticated state/equipment/map inputs
+and all relevant outputs must be bound cryptographically.
+
+Consequently the current monolithic hit relation cannot be submitted as a native
+execution proof under the enforced 4 MiB limit, even for the smallest nontrivial
+two-player case. Raising that cap alone does not satisfy transaction/transport
+bounds or the requested 30-minute/96-GiB full-match target. A narrower staged
+representation or proof composition must first preserve complete roster and map
+selection, canonical tick order and exact cryptographic state continuity. No
+financially authoritative Arena profile is enabled by this experiment.
