+# Native game build prerequisite: authority-generation migration
+
+The Arena integration starts at commit
+`8209033deae7409d800fcc576a63609a0c2c5f9d`. That snapshot already declares the
+first-release authority-generation model, but production consumers still expected
+the retired epoch-roster model. The resulting core compilation failures prevented
+building the native Connect transaction bridge.
+
+The sibling Iroha working tree was read once into an immutable local snapshot on
+2026-09-22 at 09:39:36 UTC. Fifteen files contributed reviewed prerequisite hunks.
+The adjacent [provenance record](arena_authority_generation_prerequisite.json)
+lists every source path, base/source SHA-256, selected original hunk positions,
+and combined reviewed patch SHA-256. The sibling checkout was not modified.
+The existing game allocation, deposit, and typed wrapper changes were preserved.
+This record describes a development build repair, not a release qualification.
+
+## Authority semantics
+
+- Immutable authority generations identify the ordered validator keys. A separate
+  complete authorization binds the network, scheduling epoch, governed height
+  interval, generation and authority identity, installed beacon, predecessor,
+  transition attempt, and certified decision.
+- Genesis constructs a generation-zero authorization with the exact initial
+  interval and explicit bootstrap beacon. Genesis and recursive finality pins now
+  refer to the authorization identity rather than a key-roster hash.
+- Consensus contexts and paired-Pasta seal messages carry the complete current
+  authorization and optional boundary successor. Signing and recursive proof
+  checks use the canonical authorization commitment.
+- Retention advances the scheduling epoch and height interval without relabeling
+  the incumbent key generation. The first retained interval binds the installed
+  beacon from authenticated state; later retention preserves that binding.
+- Retired next-epoch-roster parameter consumers were removed. Reward store
+  consumers were adapted to the existing separate processing-state and
+  asset-specific accrual maps. No fallback decoder or compatibility alias was
+  introduced.
+
+## Explicit remaining limitation
+
+`sumeragi/v2_context.rs` retains the incumbent committee. Its prepared E+2 committee
+activation/cancellation owner remains a TODO. The existing
+`ensure_global_candidate_pool_preserved` guard in `smartcontracts/isi/staking.rs`
+rejects unsupported changes to the active global candidate pool, rather than
+accepting a change which the context builder would discard. The model's valid
+`Activate` shape is not a certificate and does not itself authorize rotation:
+callers still need the incumbent boundary certificate, prepared target, and
+all-seat readiness evidence. This prerequisite does not qualify committee
+rotation or production monetary issuance.
+
+## Validation
+
+- Passed: `cargo check -p connect_norito_bridge --lib`, including the complete
+  production Iroha core dependency, using `scripts/cargo_fast.sh
+  --stable-local-metadata --incremental --jobs 4`. Existing unused-code warnings
+  remain. Local evidence: `target/arena-connect-check.log`.
+- Passed: both focused integration regressions named `authority_generation_migration_*`
+  in `iroha_data_model/tests/sumeragi_v2_cross_sdk_fixtures.rs`. They check complete
+  authority and predecessor binding, retention, Norito/JSON roundtrip, and exact
+  successor commitment in a boundary seal. Command: `cargo test -p iroha_data_model
+  --test iroha_data_model_group_02 authority_generation_migration -- --nocapture`;
+  evidence: `target/arena-authority-generation-tests.log`.
+- Passed: `cargo build -p connect_norito_bridge --lib` with the same local wrapper,
+  producing the macOS development dylib. Evidence: `target/arena-connect-build.log`.
+- Passed: Arena's actual C-ABI smoke script against that dylib: ABI/symbol checks,
+  strict JSON, exact-network session identity, X25519 direction keys, encrypted
+  envelope roundtrip and wrong-key/tamper/trailing-byte rejection. Native
+  Open/Join/Claim builders preserve exact authority, network, fees, and action
+  terms; 21 malformed requests and zero-signature finalization were rejected.
+  Tested dylib SHA-256:
+  `0caeb82fcfbf1119a011a8d02f58d22487db9db50947830b92013fad88a66ff0`.
+  No live wallet pairing or transaction submission was performed.
+- The initial bridge unit-test build stopped at eight retired SCCP fixture fields,
+  then two Core test-helper uses of the retired model. Those non-shipping helpers
+  now construct generation-zero authority and full genesis authorization. The
+  Core helper was reviewed from the read-only sibling source. A remaining
+  `#[cfg(test)]` Parliament finality-chain helper in the bridge was migrated to
+  the same authority model with its exact interval 1..100; real BLS quorum and
+  signed DA construction are preserved. Exact source/base/
+  isolated SHA-256 values and the bounded four-file fixture patch are recorded
+  under `test_fixture_followup` in the adjacent provenance JSON. This follow-up
+  changes no production consensus implementation and adds no compatibility alias.
+- Passed: three new Core helper regressions, compiled from the actual modified
+  helper by a focused `rustc --test` harness linked to matching production Core,
+  data-model, and crypto rlibs. They cover generation-bound real paired-Pasta keys,
+  genesis template binding, complete authorization, retention/activation, and
+  wrong-predecessor rejection. Local harness and output:
+  `target/arena-validation/authority_fixture_harness.rs` and
+  `target/arena-validation/authority-fixture-tests.log`.
+- The dependency build then passed, exposing four unsupported mutable JSON
+  indexing expressions in the existing detached-transaction rejection test.
+  Those four mutation arms now use Norito's object mutation API; malformed batch,
+  zero TTL, unsupported instruction and nested unknown-field assertions remain.
+  The extra test-only edit is recorded separately as `additional_test_api_fix`.
+- Passed: all 14 focused bridge transaction tests (zero failures, 407 filtered):
+  `scripts/cargo_fast.sh --stable-local-metadata --incremental --jobs 4 -- test
+  -p connect_norito_bridge --lib detached_transaction_scaffold_tests -- --nocapture`.
+  Output: `target/arena-validation/connect-detached-transactions-verified.log`.
+  The build completed in 5m49s; test execution took 0.13s. The suite covers exact
+  native game and marketplace terms, versioned signed payloads, actual Ed25519
+  signing/finalization, malformed input rejection, canonical JSON, and cleared
+  FFI outputs on errors. `native_transaction_` would not select this module.
+- Passed: the existing Parliament casting-proof regression using the migrated
+  finality-chain helper: one test, zero failures, 5.30s. It rejects fabricated
+  chains, wrong anchors, intermediate-block mutations and archive tampering while
+  accepting the real quorum-signed fixture. Output:
+  `target/arena-validation/connect-parliament-fixture-regression.log`.
+
+Broad model/core unit suites and old cross-SDK fixtures are not claimed as passing;
+they retain migration work outside this focused prerequisite repair. The exact
+commands, binary/log hashes and bounded fixture source identities are retained in
+the provenance JSON. All original malformed-input and finality assertions remain.
+
+The Arena damage and aim AIR experiments remain unqualified; no funded Arena
+profile is enabled by this migration.
