+# Arena 18,000-batch capacity research gate
+
+`crates/iroha_core/src/execution_proofs/arena_capacity_research.rs` is a
+bounded **unregistered** experiment for one uninterrupted 60 Hz Arena match.
+The native compiled execution catalog still contains only RaceV1. Its current
+session-opening ceiling remains 4,096 batches and 4 MiB of declared raw input
+bytes. An Arena-shaped manifest cannot pass `validate_game_manifest_v1`, cannot
+open a native session, and cannot authorize a funded bond, NFT reservation, kill
+award, or settlement. The research validator accepts the *shape* of a complete
+two-tick transcript; it does not authenticate a control byte or prove an FPS
+state transition. An altered but still 16-byte control payload deliberately
+passes the structural test to expose this boundary.
+
+The full target uses exactly `36,000 / 2 = 18,000` batches and twelve permanent
+slots. With sixteen bytes per slot and batch, its declared raw input subtotal
+is `18,000 × 12 × 16 = 3,456,000` bytes, below the existing 4,194,304-byte
+product bound by 738,304 bytes. The research preflight rejects more than
+36,000 ticks, more than twelve slots, a non-two-tick batch, a payload bound
+other than sixteen bytes, a profile other than its exact unregistered research
+identifier, a payout policy other than `NoPayout`, and the normal parameter
+bounds. Its full-history check rejects a missing or extra batch, any epoch or
+start-tick gap, a missing permanent slot, an input longer or shorter than the
+declared sixteen bytes, and DNF events. It is intentionally limited to an
+uninterrupted match; terminal-on-disconnect needs a separate proof design.
+
+The focused native codec test encodes the complete `Vec<GameForcedBatchV1>` as
+**6,030,008 canonical Norito bytes** on this revision, compared with 3,456,000
+raw control bytes. The test fixes that exact size so a layout change receives
+review. This is retained history before the rest of `GameSessionRecordV1`, not
+an inline proof envelope or a measured full snapshot/transaction cost. The
+current P2P commitment/reveal evidence has a separate 31,104,000-byte raw
+subtotal for 18,000 batches (`18,000 × 12 × (64 signature + 32 commitment +
+32 salt + 16 control)`), before wire framing or storage. Neither number is a
+verified ledger-availability measurement.
+
+The 6,030,008-byte forced-history vector alone exceeds the current 4 MiB
+execution-proof envelope, so copying the complete history into one proof is
+already impossible under that cap; segment commitments and availability are
+necessary even before accounting for a combat witness.
+
+There is a further **gas and asymptotic-cost blocker** to simply changing the
+native 4,096 check. `RevealGameInputsV1` and `CommitGameInputsV1` currently
+receive a fixed 32,000 native gas quote each, while each instruction clones the
+whole `GameSessionRecordV1` and `save` recomputes a dispute-root hash over its
+entire forced-batch vector. A fully forced 18,000-batch, twelve-slot run would
+perform 432,000 commitment/reveal instructions. Even counting only their raw
+input-history bytes, the repeated growing-history traversal has a lower-bound
+order of about `432,000 × 3,456,000 / 2 = 746,496,000,000` byte-visits,
+excluding Norito overhead, signatures, checkpoints, state writes, and proof
+verification. This is an arithmetic estimate from current source, **not** an
+observed runtime or gas measurement. The fixed quote cannot be asserted to
+cover this work. An appendable authenticated transcript, bounded per-step
+state operations, calibrated gas, retained evidence/availability, and proof
+composition are required before a production Arena capacity path is safe.
+
+The existing 4 MiB execution-proof envelope also remains unchanged. Neither
+the standalone Arena damage proof nor the single-axis geometry experiment
+proves complete combat, the full accepted history, a kill, or allocation.
+Extending the session batch ceiling is therefore held behind the complete
+ArenaV1 relation and independent full-size proving/validator cost gates.
+
+Focused check (unfunded research only):
+
+```sh
+cargo test --locked --offline -j2 -p iroha_core --features iroha-core-tests --test arena_capacity_research -- --nocapture
+```
