@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Arena 26-tick signed-history kill research (unregistered)
+
+This is a bounded research proof for one three-player, two-shooter FFA scene. It is **not** `ArenaV1`, a funded game session, an NFT admission, a selected ledger history, or an XOR settlement authority. `compiled_execution_profile_v1` rejects its profile ID and the generic admission-bound genesis API does not dispatch to it. The saved 25-tick kill research proof remains unchanged: SHA-256 `577d706dc0d0d2396c412b817c490c08bab4bef655b0d3bdc65e2c8b84562e49`.
+
+## Statement and proof boundary
+
+`arena_kill_history_research.rs` carries one public statement with the isolated network and session, exact immutable three-slot admission, 2-tick/max-26 manifest, admission-derived research genesis, manifest and roster hashes, manually specified restricted map/rules/equipment commitments, all 13 signed commitment sets, 39 slot signatures, 39 salted reveals and 78 complete eight-byte controls. It independently derives the game's SHA-256 P2P rolling root and Iroha's Norito native transcript root from those same accepted controls, and checks 13 caller-supplied native batch projections against them. These two roots are different domains. Neither root is selected from ledger-retained evidence in this test.
+
+The separate [pure history-translation research](arena_history_translation_research_v1.md) derives sequential native batch epochs and conditional dispute-root components from the same signed controls. It does not change this saved proof or supply ledger-selected evidence.
+
+Native host validation checks the exact restricted 26-frame input scene, including the game's `-127..=127` move-axis, pitch and button bounds. It rejects altered admission, deposits, weapons, map/rules/equipment commitments, signatures, batch order, roots, native projections, projected boundaries, targets and payout allocations. The full public statement and source-sealed Iroha relation enter the STARK public-input digest. The native AIR proves 60 wall/body slab arithmetic stages and 26 projected combat/economic tick transitions. Signed FIRE bits are checked against AIR fixed columns. The final committed idle tick is included: the victim's respawn timer changes `480 -> 479`, both shooters' cooldowns change `12 -> 11`, and terminal changes `false -> true`. A 128-stage period contains 26 tick stages, 60 geometry stages and 42 copies of a valid neutral geometry stage; 128 divides the 8,192-row trace, so no active tick chain crosses the physical wrap.
+
+The proof constrains the fields in `KillResearchStateV1`, not the entire `arena_core::World`. Input signatures, exact non-FIRE control bytes, admission equality, slab selection and outcome identity are verifier-side public checks bound by the statement digest; they are not general AIR execution of arbitrary game rules. A fixed [22-damage arc-carbine scene](../../crates/iroha_core/src/execution_proofs/arena_kill_history_research.rs) is compiled manually. The `sora-arena-first-release-6` label and the game fixture's source fingerprint are **drift checks**, not a cryptographic binding to the complete live kernel or catalog. A changed live damage rule could diverge from this relation until source-derived profile identity and full semantics are added.
+
+## Reproduction and measurements on M1 Ultra
+
+The focused integration test `arena_kill_history_research` passed: 795 AIR columns, 1,729 constraints, conservative maximum STARK wire 2,914,432 bytes, and conservative full encoded `ExecutionProofEnvelopeV1` maximum **2,946,649 bytes**, below the enforced 4,194,304-byte native envelope cap. The actual bare STARK artifact is [`target/arena-kill-history-research/history-kill.stark`](../../target/arena-kill-history-research/history-kill.stark), 2,772,064 bytes, SHA-256 `69a776cdbe26b04b176aab5a23f7c5ecd8654284a1f0559bbf421b898905b2af`. The repository does not save or submit a custody-authorizing envelope for it.
+
+The corrected proof took 169.685 s to produce. Prove plus in-process verify took 187.53 s wall time and 768,720,896 bytes maximum resident memory. Verification in a fresh process took 18.081 s for the valid artifact; valid verification plus four tamper checks took 32.73 s wall time and 43,925,504 bytes maximum resident memory. The separate process rejected a changed host-valid geometry fraction at STARK verification, altered native input projection, changed final respawn value, and a corrupted proof byte. The fast test also rejected reordered/omitted batches, altered parent/start/signature/salt/final frame, invalid `-128` on either movement axis, a **properly re-signed** legal nonzero movement frame or final FIRE frame that conflicts with the fixed scene, altered identities/admission/state/award/target, and found zero raw AIR stage residues. The relation source/test fingerprints were unchanged during the successful prove.
+
+The independent game-kernel replay fixture in `sora-arena` commit `ded8806` is `crates/arena-core/tests/data/arena_kill_history_v2_kernel.json`. Its kernel source SHA-256 is `f2d9bb091202725a5cf890ae58580b44fdb88227313e6462660784ff4b5960c9`. Comparing that fixture with this relation found **zero mismatches** across all 27 projected boundaries, all 78 control frames and final allocations `[1020,1080,900]`. The fixture is a regression tripwire for the manually fixed relation; it is not included as a source-derived Arena execution profile or a production identity.
+
+## Remaining gates
+
+The admitted 1,000-unit deposits are research values only. The relation does not fetch selected input history or custody state from the ledger, prove general collision/movement/abilities/hits, establish NFT entitlement, prove arbitrary kills or payouts, prevent aimbots/collusion, or authorize any transfer. Production `ArenaV1` still needs source-bound full-state execution, ledger-selected canonical evidence and disconnect rules, per-kill conservation for variable bonds/team modes, catalog and equipment checks, and qualification at the agreed full match size. The current 4,096-batch ceiling also does not cover a 36,000-tick match at two ticks per batch. Do not register this research profile or enable real-value bonding on its evidence.
+
+The wider Iroha worktree contains prior `proof.rs` edits that change the source-derived Race profile ID. Existing Race settlements require retained historical compiled verification before deployment, regardless of the new Arena release's no-legacy policy.
