+# Two-tick Arena kill-history audit (unregistered)
+
+`crates/iroha_core/tests/arena_kill_two_tick_history.rs` independently mirrors the current `arena-core::protocol` P2P hash framing: the context domain, two eight-byte controls per slot, salted input commitments that include the prior transcript root, three Ed25519 signatures over the joint commitment set, and the ordered reveal transcript-root update. It builds thirteen contiguous batches covering ticks 0–25. Batches 0–11 and the first frame of batch 12 reproduce all 25 source-sealed kill-scene controls. The second frame of batch 12 is idle padding, because the local game protocol requires exactly two frames per batch.
+
+The matching game source for this audit is `sora-arena/crates/arena-core/src/protocol.rs` at SHA-256 `a0eb3a155af9e5b3dfcdbfcdb766dd5e2046a93429f92909312d214baab5dcaf`. The test does not depend on a sibling checkout at build time; recheck the mirror when that game protocol changes.
+
+The audit checks every slot signature and reveal against its commitment, all start ticks and parent roots, the flattened controls against `canonical_input_v1`, and all twelve mutable projected state links between consecutive rows from `reference_tick_rows_v1`. The final volley occurs at tick 24 and the proven projected boundary at tick 25 is HP 0, victim reserve 900, assist earnings 20, and killer earnings 80. Deliberate parent, tick, signature, reveal, slot, network and lethal-control changes are rejected by either history authentication or the AIR-input comparison.
+
+This is **host-side research evidence**. The saved 25-tick native STARK in `arena_kill_research_v1.md` binds one 25-tick research-batch statement and its frozen source. This new thirteen-batch history is not inside that proof's public-input digest, and the final padded tick is not inside that AIR. The separate two-tick research manifest has no registered execution profile and no funds. The test mirrors the game P2P protocol's byte layout but does not turn a peer transcript into a consensus-selected Iroha history. No custody, market, wallet or value transfer is enabled by this audit.
+
+The next implementation step is a registered general `ArenaV1` execution relation whose statement binds the ledger-selected two-tick transcript, admission, complete kernel state and terminal awards, followed by full-match proving and four-validator settlement qualification.
