+# Arena signed sidestep-to-kill research (unregistered)
+
+`arena_moved_kill_research.rs` is a two-tick, three-participant fixed-scene
+experiment. Its profile is deliberately absent from the compiled registry:
+`compiled_execution_profile_v1` cannot resolve it, and
+`initial_game_state_root_v1` rejects its manifest. It cannot admit a funded
+match, reserve equipment, or authorize XOR settlement.
+
+The public statement binds an isolated network and session, exact three-slot
+admission with 1,000-unit deposits, a manually restricted rules hash, a fixed
+research checkpoint tag, one complete three-party P2P commitment set, all
+three Ed25519 signatures and salted 16-byte reveals, the corresponding native
+two-tick batch, both transcript roots, and terminal allocations. Host
+validation verifies those signatures and projections and fixes every control
+except the blocker's first-tick forward axis, an unsigned integer from 0 to
+127. The shooter fires only on tick zero. The second tick is signed idle input.
+The checkpoint tag is **not selected or authenticated by ledger consensus**.
+
+The native integer AIR constrains the blocker's cardinal +Y movement as
+`350 + trunc(axis × 80 / 127)` millimetres. The fixed +X shot intersects the
+blocker's closed body at `y = 350` and clears it when the new Y coordinate is
+greater than 350. The AIR links that comparison to target slot, one 22-damage
+hit, surviving/dead health, the dead target's second-tick respawn timer,
+100-unit loss from its original 1,000-unit reserve, the shooter's separate
+100-unit earned credit, and exact conservation. The host checks that the
+terminal allocation vector matches those proved reserve and credit claims.
+The example with axis 0 hits the blocker (health 103, no death reward); axis
+127 clears the blocker and kills the 22-health target (reserve 900, shooter
+award 1,100 including returned bond).
+
+The fixed checkpoint positions, low initial target health, body radius, x/z
+ordering, clear map corridor, weapon eligibility and damage, spawn protection,
+first-tick fire permission, second-tick idle behavior, and every other game
+state component are **scene premises or verifier-side checks**, not general
+AIR execution. This does not prove arbitrary movement, world collision,
+weapon effects, simultaneous attacks, objectives, assists, team allocation,
+variable bonds, NFTs, disconnect resolution, or a canonical ledger-selected
+input history. The proof digest binds this research statement and adapter
+source, not the complete live `arena-core` kernel. The two signed ticks are
+included in the statement, but the AIR does not model all second-tick state
+transitions. A valid proof would establish only the listed bounded equations.
+
+The focused integration test is `--test arena_moved_kill_research`. It includes
+five legal move amounts, adversarial claim and signature mutations, native
+AIR residue checks, conservative wire preflight, and an ignored full native
+prover/verifier roundtrip. At the time of this change, the disk was below the
+20 GiB build floor and other Cargo jobs were active, so **the new code has only
+been formatted and source-reviewed; no Cargo test or native proof has run**.
+Do not count this as a successful end-to-end proof or a qualified match gate.
