+# Arena movement proof research (unregistered)
+
+`arena_movement_research.rs` is a bounded, unfunded proof experiment. Its exact
+manifest admits two Samurai with team, class, weapon, and bond all zero,
+no wagers or equipment,
+map zero, and `offline=true`. The generic `GameAdmissionBodyV1` is checked before
+the domain-separated research genesis root is derived. The native compiled
+registry has no Arena entry: `OpenGameSessionV1` and the generic
+`initial_game_state_root_v1` reject this profile. Neither a wallet nor custody
+can join, bond, reserve an NFT, or settle from this relation.
+
+The public statement binds network and session identities, the exact manifest
+and immutable admission, map-wall and movement-rule hashes, peer-signed
+individual input commitments, a jointly signed commitment set rooted in the
+research genesis, their opening salts and input payloads, one canonical
+`GameForcedBatchV1`-shaped batch, and positions at ticks zero, one, and two.
+This is a **peer-accepted research batch**, not a consensus-selected native
+forced batch. Without a compiled Arena profile and native admission, the
+ledger cannot authenticate its selection or use the proof for settlement.
+
+Each 16-byte per-player payload contains two ordinary eight-byte Arena inputs.
+The research verifier admits only buttons zero, `move_y=0`, pitch zero, and
+cardinal yaw. Each input has `move_x` in the kernel's exact `-127..=127`
+range; encoded `-128` is rejected.
+The fixed-point AIR constrains the exact Samurai movement quotient
+`trunc(move_x × 80 / 127)`, cardinal rotation, and x/y accumulation for each
+player and tick. The verifier checks initial spawns and a maximum 80 mm movement
+radius per tick. Map-zero walls lie within x ±8,000 mm, whereas both spawns
+are at x ±18,000 mm; the entire two-tick corridor is collision-free and inside
+world bounds. This establishes a real, restricted, outcome-affecting position
+transition without treating an unconstrained position claim as a proof.
+
+The relation does not prove attacks, hit selection, deaths, objectives, XOR
+losses/awards, NFT entitlement, or a full game state. It cannot imply a
+qualified match profile. `offline=true` and zero bond are required by the Arena
+kernel; switching to a live-funded match would fail closed. Full 6v6 and
+ten-minute proving remain open feasibility gates.
+
+The reference fixture was also run through the current `arena-core`
+`World::step` under `RULES_VERSION=sora-arena-first-release-6`. The two
+positions at ticks zero, one, and two were `(18000, 0), (-18000, 0)`;
+`(18080, 0), (-17960, 0)`; and `(18080, 40), (-17960, 80)` millimetres,
+matching the research statement exactly.
+
+Run the focused integration test with `--test arena_movement_research`. The
+two explicitly ignored tests generate and independently verify a saved proof
+when `ARENA_MOVEMENT_PROOF_PATH` points to a local test artifact. Record actual
+wire bytes, prove and verify time, peak resident memory, and the native
+preflight maximum before considering any expansion. Do not register this profile
+or turn on funding based on these results.
+
+On the available M1 Ultra with the native Iroha DEEP-ALI/FRI backend, the
+compiled AIR has 81 columns and 90 constraints; the native preflight maximum
+is 1,315,072 bytes, below the existing 4 MiB wire cap. The final proof for
+the exact all-zero team/class/weapon/bond admission was **1,192,288 bytes**
+(SHA-256 `2456130dad1254c76e73665c406a5bff5b58d46b884c3b59e894bb0582b2d0b5`).
+Proving took 121,994 ms with 252,723,200 bytes peak resident memory. A
+separate process accepted the saved proof in 12,260 ms with 24,870,912 bytes
+peak resident memory, and rejected modified positions, input, session
+identity, and proof bytes. The focused admission/history test passed and
+rejected altered bond, equipment, attack input, reveal, signatures, map, and
+rules identity. These are **two-tick research costs**, not full-match
+qualification or an estimate of 6v6 ten-minute proving.
+
+The earlier admission-bound genesis API change also edits `proof.rs`, which is
+in the **source-derived Race profile ID**. Valid Race initial state roots remain
+unchanged, but the profile ID changes. An Iroha deployment with outstanding
+Race sessions would need a versioned compiled historical Race verifier before
+installing this worktree; the new Arena project's first-release no-legacy rule
+does not erase those existing settlement obligations.
