+# Arena ranged-hit proof research (unregistered)
+
+This experiment proves one restricted, genesis-derived Arc carbine hit in the
+current `sora-arena-first-release-6` reference kernel. It is an **unregistered,
+offline, zero-bond** Iroha Core relation. The generic compiled registry still
+contains Race only; no game session can accept the research profile or use its
+proof for custody, an NFT entitlement, a kill payout, or XOR settlement.
+
+The exact admission has three Samurai in FFA on map zero. All teams and deposits
+are zero; slot 0 has standard weapon 1 (Arc carbine), and slots 1 and 2 have
+standard weapon 0 (katana). One jointly signed, peer-accepted batch contains
+**two canonical ticks** per slot. Slot 0 fires at yaw 24576 on tick zero and
+everyone is idle on tick one. Its first eight input bytes are
+`01 00 00 00 00 60 00 00`; every other eight-byte input is zero. The statement
+binds network, session, immutable manifest and admission, input commitments,
+joint signatures, salts, reveals, the complete batch, map and restricted rules
+hashes, and projected states at ticks zero, one, and two. The commitment set is
+rooted in an admission-bound research genesis. Peers signed the batch; **the
+ledger did not select it**.
+
+The native STARK uses one staged trace: 30 ordered slab-endpoint rows for all
+three map walls and both eligible player bodies, plus one damage row. Each slab
+row is constrained by the existing exact `arena_geometry_air::plane_v1` AIR.
+The damage row is constrained by `arena_damage_air::ArenaDamageAirV1`.
+Verifier-fixed stage markers select the relevant constraint set for each row;
+the full public statement and exact relation source are bound to the proof
+transcript. The verifier reduces the proved public slab fractions in map-wall
+order, then eligible player-slot order, with strict-less nearest-hit ties. It
+derives slot 2 as the selected victim; the target cannot be a free witness. It
+binds damage 22 and health 125→103 to that selection and the outgoing public
+state projection. The second tick keeps health 103, ammo 23, and decreases the
+shooter cooldown 12→11; the research session then becomes terminal. The
+current Arena Rust kernel was run independently with these inputs and produced
+the same hit, damage, history, ammo, cooldown and terminal state. The parity run
+used the exact all-team-zero admission and an `arena-core` library rebuilt after
+the current version-6 source. There is no cross-platform or independent
+implementation parity claim.
+
+The fixed `RULES` byte string is a **manually maintained restricted research
+specification**. Its hash is not a cryptographic commitment to all
+`arena-core` source. The fixed yaw/ray and reference-kernel parity cover this
+one fixture only; arbitrary yaw, weapon choice, movement, objectives, status
+effects, kills and funds are outside the relation. Host-side validation checks
+the exact canonical input pattern, immutable scene coordinates, public state
+projection, signatures and tie reduction; AIR proves slab fractions and damage
+arithmetic. The projection is not the complete Arena `World` state. A funded
+profile needs source-bound rules semantics, consensus-selected history, proof
+coverage of every outcome-affecting transition, and full qualification. No
+full-match cost or security conclusion follows from this experiment.
+
+Run the focused `--test arena_ranged_research` integration target for admission,
+history, missing-wall, alternate-target, forged-occlusion, damage and state
+mutations. Its proof and separate-verifier tests are explicitly ignored by
+default and require `ARENA_RANGED_PROOF_PATH` to point to a local artifact.
+The native 4 MiB wire cap is enforced by preflight before any proving run.
+
+On the available M1 Ultra, the focused profile compiled to 658 arithmetic
+columns and 1,414 constraints. The conservative encoded-proof maximum was
+2,607,552 bytes, below the 4,194,304-byte native limit. An actual proof of the
+fixed two-tick scene was 2,471,808 bytes and took 134,148 ms in the prove call;
+the prove-and-self-verify test process took 151.31 seconds and peaked at
+664,354,816 bytes resident. A fresh process verified the saved proof in
+17,426 ms; its verification and negative-mutation test process took 26.04
+seconds and peaked at 35,487,744 bytes resident. The artifact is
+`target/arena-ranged-research/ranged.stark`, SHA-256
+`f7e626081cf1938d388876129ab591681029835756be7a17041a76523a8a76cd`.
+The fresh-process test rejects altered target, a plausible but false slab
+fraction, altered damage, altered input and a corrupted proof. Exact-state and
+scene mutations are rejected by deterministic host validation; the unchanged
+proof rejects the otherwise host-valid fraction mutation through the public
+transcript digest. These tests do not establish general FPS transition
+soundness or full-match proving cost.
+
+The admission-bound genesis change in `proof.rs` also changes the source-derived
+Race profile ID. Any deployment from this worktree must provide versioned
+historical verification for outstanding Race sessions. Arena's first-release
+no-legacy policy does not cancel existing Race settlement obligations.
